hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2754","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa‘id, narrated to us Ja‘far, who said: My father narrated to me, who said:\nWe came to Jabir ibn ‘Abd Allah and asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ). He then mentioned the hadith at length and said:\n“When the Prophet (ﷺ) finished his circumambulation (tawāf), he went directly to the Station of Ibrahim and prayed two rak‘ahs behind it, reciting:\n‘And take, [O believers], from the Station of Ibrahim a place of prayer’ (Qur’an 2:125).\nHe said: ‘He would recite in them Surah al-Tawḥīd (Qul Huwa Allāhu Aḥad) and Surah al-Kāfirūn (Qul Yā Ayyuhā al-Kāfirūn).’”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
